e AI systems that automate complex hardware engineering workflows. You will develop novel agents that interpret and manipulate design data, integrating them into production environments for enterprise customers. This high\\-impact role offers the chance to build foundational infrastructure for world\\-changing industries from the ground up.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Location**\n San Francisco, USA\n   \n\n  \n\n**Why this role is remarkable**\n* Rare opportunity to join a top\\-tier VC\\-backed startup as one of the first technical hires with significant ownership.\n* You will work at the cutting edge of AI, building agents that solve physical\\-world engineering challenges rather than just digital tasks.\n* The role offers direct influence over the engineering culture, technical architecture, and long\\-term product roadmap of the company.\n\n\n**What You Will Do**\n* Design and implement intelligent context management and novel indexing approaches for hardware engineering agents.\n* Build and post\\-train ML models capable of reasoning over complex geometric and engineering design data.\n* Collaborate directly with enterprise customers to ensure AI\\-powered workflows are reliable and trusted in production.\n\n\n**The ideal candidate**\n* Holds a degree in Computer Science or Machine Learning with strong proficiency in LLM architectures and agent research.\n* Proven track record of building and shipping production\\-grade ML systems using PyTorch or Hugging Face.\n* Exceptional programming skills with practical experience in search, information retrieval, or geometric data processing.\n\n\n**Who are Jack \\& Jill?**\n Ok, I'll go first. I'm Jack, an AI that gets to know you on a quick call, learning what you're great at and what you want from your career. Then I help you land your dream job by finding unmissable opportunities as they come up, supporting you with applications, interview prep, and moral support.\n   \n\n  \n\n And I'm Jill, an AI Recruiter who talks to companies to understand who they're looking to hire. Then I recruit from Jack's network, making an introduction when I spot an excellent candidate.\n   \n\n  \n\n**How does this work?**\n* Jack's an AI agent for job searching and career coaching. He works for you.\n* Jill is the AI recruiter working for the company. She recruits from Jack's network.\n* If it's a match and the company wants to meet you, they'll make the intro. In the meantime, if you'd like, Jack will send you excellent alternatives.\n\n\n**We never post fake jobs**\n This isn't a trick. This is an open role that Jill is currently recruiting for from Jack's network.\n   \n\n  \n\n Sometimes Jill's clients ask her to anonymize their jobs when she advertises them, which means she can't share all the details in the job description.\n   \n\n  \n\n We appreciate this can make them look a bit suspect, but there isn't much we can do about it.\n   \n\n  \n\n Give Jack a spin! You could land this role. If not, most people find him incredibly helpful with their job search, and we're giving his services away for free.","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4425563240":"**AGI Algorithmic Software Engineer** \n\n  \n \n\n\n\n\n*Fully Remote • Global Candidates Welcome* \n\n  \n \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Want to be part of the core team building the technology that will leapfrog LLMs?** \n  \n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n We have developed and previously commercialized an AI that requires a million times less training data than LLMs, trains and runs on a single off\\-the\\-shelf computer, and learns and adapts incrementally in real time. The approach, called Cognitive AI, is based on first principles of human cognition and overcomes the cost, reliability, privacy, and security limitations of LLMs.  \n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n We are now on the final stretch of scaling this technology to full general adult\\-level ability and to bring it to the world. A multi\\-trillion\\-dollar opportunity.   \n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n If this vision excites you and you are available to fully dedicate yourself to our mission, read on. \n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n The team is motivated by the positive vision of how Cognitive AI can foster human flourishing, the challenge of solving difficult novel problems, and the rewards that come from building something truly transformative.  \n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Financial compensation of this core team leans more towards meaningful stock options than maximizing cash. Think early Google or SpaceX, employee \\#15\\. \n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n \n\n\n\n**The Role** \n  \n \n\n\n\n This is not a role maintaining existing products or optimizing existing AI models. You will work directly with Aigo’s chief scientist and engineering team to bring innovative core algorithms to life.  \n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Prior AI experience is not required—our approach differs substantially from traditional machine learning, rule\\-based systems, and large language models. What matters most is your ability to excel at algorithmic design, development, optimization, and problem\\-solving. If you’re also fascinated by the nature of intelligence and comfortable thinking like a cognitive scientist, that’s a real advantage. \n \n\n\n\n  \n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Requirements:** \n  \n \n\n\n* 2\\+ years of professional software engineering experience\n* Proven strength in algorithm design, development, optimization, and debugging complex systems\n* Strong analytical thinking and logical problem\\-solving skills\n* Proficiency in C\\# (.NET Core)—or the ability to quickly become fluent\n* Comfortable working in a fast\\-moving, highly iterative environment where the problem itself is still being solved\n* Hacker\\-at\\-heart: you solve problems, you don’t wait for them to be solved for you\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**What’s Not Required:** \n  \n \n\n\n\n*Prior AI/ML, full\\-stack, cloud, communications, or security expertise. This role is all about core algorithms and deep system\\-level coding.* \n\n  \n \n\n\n\n\n  \n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Interested?** \n\n\n\n\n\n Click Apply to visit our careers page and follow the application instructions at the bottom of the posting.","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4425556174":"**This is a job that Jill, our AI Recruiter, is recruiting for on behalf of one of our customers.**\n She will pick the best candidates from Jack's network.\n   \n\n  \n\n The next step is to speak to Jack.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Job Title**\n AI Engineer\n   \n\n  \n\n**Salary**\n $150,000 \\- $300,000 \\+ Equity\n   \n\n  \n\n**Company Description**\n 776 and Neo\\-backed AI startup democratizing software creation with $150k\\-$300k base salaries.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Job Description**\n Join a high\\-caliber team of engineers from Google and OpenAI to build the world's most capable consumer\\-facing coding agent. You will bridge the gap between human intent and software execution by designing agentic architectures that turn ideas into native mobile applications instantly. This is a chance to redefine software creation for millions.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Location**\n New York, USA\n   \n\n  \n\n**Why this role is remarkable**\n* Backed by elite investors including Alexis Ohanian (776\\), Neo, and leaders from OpenAI and Google.\n* Work alongside a world\\-class team with backgrounds from Bluesky, Docker, Nuro, and Google in a high\\-intensity NYC office.\n* Massive ownership and significant equity (up to 2%) at a seed\\-stage startup aiming to make coding obsolete for creators.\n\n\n**What You Will Do**\n* Design and implement state\\-of\\-the\\-art agentic architectures for a consumer\\-facing coding AI agent using TypeScript.\n* Build robust evaluation frameworks to measure code quality and ensure perfect alignment with user intent.\n* Work across the entire AI stack from model architecture to production deployment to ship magical user experiences.\n\n\n**The ideal candidate**\n* 3\\+ years of experience building and deploying production\